SDL2: never resize a fullscreen window on guest mode changes.

On SDL's kmsdrm backend, SDL_SetWindowSize on a fullscreen window rebuilds
the GBM/EGL surfaces and the opengl/opengles2 renderer keeps presenting to
the old ones, so the panel stays black after the first guest mode switch.
A fullscreen window already scales through SDL_RenderSetLogicalSize.

--- ./ui/sdl2.c
+++ ./ui/sdl2.c
@@ -143,7 +143,7 @@
 
 void sdl2_window_resize(struct sdl2_console *scon)
 {
-    if (!scon->real_window) {
+    if (!scon->real_window || gui_fullscreen) {
         return;
     }
 
